A||||3||ponya||Battery problem||||5||
Z||000000||ponya||09-11-2000||07:34 PM||||I took the car for a ride this morning and when I returned I pulled into the garage to do a little work on it. I had checked all the gauges when I went for my ride and everything was normal. Worked on the car all day and when I was done, I just happened to look under the car and I saw something wet in front of the right rear wheel. I thought it was water, but when I felt it, it had that distinct feel and smell of acid. Took out the battery and saw that battery acid was coming out of the filler caps. It had obviously been doing this for awhile, because I now saw when it had been dripping down. Took off the caps and the water seemed high. I know I had taken water out about a month ago when I checked and thought it was too high. I took out more water, to just above the plates and went for a ride. Got home and thought all was OK but I heard what sounded like water under pressure. Sure enough, the top of the battery was wet again. If I take out any more water, I will expose the plates. <BR>Any idea's what's wrong? Battery bad? Any info or idea's appreciated. Thanks, Bob||||reg||5
Z||000001||hugh||09-11-2000||07:41 PM||||yOU PROBABLY NEED A BATTERY,IT MAY BE CAUSED BY A BAD VOLTAGE REGULATOR MAKING THE ALTERNATOR CHARGE TOO MUCH.iF YOU HAVE ACCESS TO A VOLT METER PUT IT ON YOUR BATTERY POSTS WHEN THE CAR IS RUNNING,THE VOLTAGE SHOULD NOT BE ABOVE ABOUT 14 VOLTS MAXIMUM. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||webbee||09-11-2000||07:50 PM||||Sounds like a voltage regulator/alternator problem. Overcharging is most likly. Take it to a shop and have them check the charging circut. You may need to replace the alternator. It also could be heat or a bad battery. Be sure to wash the area with baking soda/h2o mix and then hose with h2o, to neutralise the acid. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||09-11-2000||10:15 PM||||That battery is definatly fried. What else may be bad you'll find when you have the charging system tested. Do this ASAP. Driving it like this can fry the whole car.||||reg||1
